### Reading a Value of Type T from a Byte Array

Here's an example implementation in Java that reads a value of type `T` from a byte array. This implementation uses Java's built-in `ByteBuffer` class to efficiently read the value.

```java
import java.nio.ByteBuffer;
import java.nio.ByteOrder;
import java.io.IOException;

public class ValueReader<T> {

    /**
     * Reads a value of type T from the specified byte array.
     * 
     * @param bytes the byte array containing the value to read
     * @return the read value of type T
     * @throws IOException if an I/O error occurs during the read operation
     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if the byte array is invalid or incomplete
     */
    public T readValue(byte[] bytes) throws IOException {
        if (bytes == null || bytes.length == 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid or empty byte array");
        }

        ByteBuffer buffer = ByteBuffer.wrap(bytes);
        buffer.order(ByteOrder.BIG_ENDIAN); // Use big-endian byte order by default

        // Determine the type of the value based on the byte array length
        switch (bytes.length) {
            case 1:
                return (T) readByte(buffer);
            case 2:
                return (T) readShort(buffer);
            case 4:
                return (T) readInt(buffer);
            case 8:
                return (T) readLong(buffer);
            default:
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unsupported byte array length");
        }
    }

    private byte readByte(ByteBuffer buffer) {
        return buffer.get();
    }

    private short readShort(ByteBuffer buffer) {
        return buffer.getShort();
    }

    private int readInt(ByteBuffer buffer) {
        return buffer.getInt();
    }

    private long readLong(ByteBuffer buffer) {
        return buffer.getLong();
    }
}
```

### Example Usage

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ValueReader<Integer> reader = new ValueReader<>();

        byte[] bytes = {0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x04};
        try {
            Integer value = reader.readValue(bytes);
            System.out.println("Read value: " + value);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("Error reading value: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
