### CorsHandler Class

#### Overview

The `CorsHandler` class is responsible for handling Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) requests. It takes a CORS configuration object as a parameter and uses it to determine the allowed origins, methods, headers, and other settings for CORS requests.

#### Constructor

```javascript
/**
 * Initializes a new instance of the CorsHandler with the specified CORS configuration.
 *
 * @param {Object} config - The CORS configuration to use.
 * @param {string} [config.allowedOrigins] - The allowed origins for CORS requests.
 * @param {string[]} [config.allowedMethods] - The allowed HTTP methods for CORS requests.
 * @param {string[]} [config.allowedHeaders] - The allowed HTTP headers for CORS requests.
 * @param {string} [config.exposedHeaders] - The exposed HTTP headers for CORS requests.
 * @param {number} [config.maxAge] - The maximum age for CORS requests.
 * @param {boolean} [config.credentials] - Whether to include credentials in CORS requests.
 */
function CorsHandler(config) {
  this.config = config;
  this.allowedOrigins = config.allowedOrigins;
  this.allowedMethods = config.allowedMethods || ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'];
  this.allowedHeaders = config.allowedHeaders || ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'];
  this.exposedHeaders = config.exposedHeaders || 'Content-Type';
  this.maxAge = config.maxAge || 3600; // 1 hour
  this.credentials = config.credentials || false;
}
```

#### Usage Example

```javascript
const corsConfig = {
  allowedOrigins: 'http://example.com',
  allowedMethods: ['GET', 'POST'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  exposedHeaders: 'Content-Type',
  maxAge: 7200, // 2 hours
  credentials: true
};

const corsHandler = new CorsHandler(corsConfig);
```

